<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Dashboard xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- M4-S02. The VP's tile: the whole open Enterprise pipeline by close month (requirement.md
         item 5, Q24). dashboardType SpecifiedUser per Q24 and D7. NO runningUser element (A29): no
         answer supplies the VP's username, and on deploy the platform fills an undefined runningUser
         with the DEPLOYING user's username. Setting it is a mandatory pre-deploy step,
         deploy-order.md section 6. A SpecifiedUser dashboard shows every viewer the running user's
         data regardless of their own security settings.
         The component re-reads the source report: chartSummary column Opportunity$Amount (U1, code 3)
         and groupingColumn Opportunity$CloseDate (U1, code 5) are the same provisional codes as the
         report, UNVERIFIED (2026-10-02). Charting the report's second grouping alone, and the
         autoselectColumnsFromReport element name, are UNVERIFIED (2026-10-02), U9. The component
         shape is the Metadata API guide's own SpecifiedUser dashboard sample. The right section is
         empty on purpose (one tile asked for; components is optional), UNVERIFIED (2026-10-02), U10.
         Repair after MOCK-DEPLOY-M4 run 1 (N4-F-03): the org requires sortBy on a chart component.
         sortBy is RowLabelAscending, from the guide's DashboardComponentFilter enumeration (alphabetical
         order by the label, here the close-month label of the tile's grouping).
         Repair after MOCK-DEPLOY-M4 run 2 (N4-F-04): the org requires chartAxisRange on a chart component.
         chartAxisRange is Auto, as the guide's samples and the skill's dashboard example write it; the guide's
         ChartRangeType table lists the value as lowercase auto. The case differs between the guide's table and
         its samples; the samples' form is used and the org judges.
         No dashboard filter (A41), no subscription (A30), current snapshot only (A42). -->
    <backgroundEndColor>#FFFFFF</backgroundEndColor>
    <backgroundFadeDirection>Diagonal</backgroundFadeDirection>
    <backgroundStartColor>#FFFFFF</backgroundStartColor>
    <chartTheme>light</chartTheme>
    <colorPalette>colorSafe</colorPalette>
    <dashboardType>SpecifiedUser</dashboardType>
    <description>The whole open Enterprise pipeline by close month for the VP. Runs as one specified user, so every viewer sees that user's data; the folder is limited to the Enterprise Managers group.</description>
    <leftSection>
        <columnSize>Wide</columnSize>
        <components>
            <autoselectColumnsFromReport>false</autoselectColumnsFromReport>
            <chartAxisRange>Auto</chartAxisRange>
            <chartSummary>
                <aggregate>Sum</aggregate>
                <axisBinding>y</axisBinding>
                <column>Opportunity$Amount</column>
            </chartSummary>
            <componentType>Column</componentType>
            <displayUnits>Auto</displayUnits>
            <drillEnabled>true</drillEnabled>
            <drillToDetailEnabled>false</drillToDetailEnabled>
            <enableHover>true</enableHover>
            <groupingColumn>Opportunity$CloseDate</groupingColumn>
            <header>Enterprise pipeline</header>
            <legendPosition>Bottom</legendPosition>
            <report>Enterprise_Sales/Open_Enterprise_Pipeline_By_Stage</report>
            <showValues>true</showValues>
            <sortBy>RowLabelAscending</sortBy>
            <title>Open pipeline by close month</title>
            <useReportChart>false</useReportChart>
        </components>
    </leftSection>
    <rightSection>
        <columnSize>Narrow</columnSize>
    </rightSection>
    <textColor>#000000</textColor>
    <title>Enterprise Pipeline</title>
    <titleColor>#000000</titleColor>
    <titleSize>12</titleSize>
</Dashboard>
